        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ab266f18-4da2-5724-8388-56f9a4230d3a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gene Kelly, Eugene Curran Kelly, Rosemary Lane, Liza Minnelli, Abbott\n- Works: Best Foot Forward, Flora the Red Menace, The Dangerous Christmas of Red Riding Hood, Cabaret, Liza with a \"Z\" (A Concert for Television), Lucky Lady, A Matter of Time, New York, New York, The Act, The Rink, Stepping Out, Music from The Life: A New Musical, Sex and the City 2\n- Topics: musical theatre, choreography, discography\n\nFacts:\n- Eugene Curran Kelly was born on August 23, 1912, and he became an American dancer, actor for film, stage, and television, singer, film director, producer, and choreographer.\n- Best Foot Forward was directed by Abbott, choreographed by Gene Kelly, and starred Rosemary Lane.\n- Liza Minnelli contributed to the original cast recording of Best Foot Forward in 1963.\n- Liza Minnelli contributed to original cast recordings for Flora the Red Menace in 1965, The Dangerous Christmas of Red Riding Hood in 1965, The Act in 1977, and The Rink in 1984.\n- Liza Minnelli contributed to soundtrack albums for Cabaret in 1972, Liza with a \"Z\" (A Concert for Television) in 1972, Lucky Lady in 1975, A Matter of Time in 1976, New York, New York in 1977, Stepping Out in 1991, Music from The Life: A New Musical in 1995, and Sex and the City 2 in 2010.\n- Eugene Curran Kelly died on February 2, 1996.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
